      "text": "A neutron is composed of one up (u) quark and two down (d) quarks. When the neutron decays to a proton, there is $\\beta$-emission."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "What is the change in the quark structure of the neutron due to the $\\beta$-emission?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(The symbol for a neutrino is $\\nu_\\text{e}$ and for an antineutrino is $\\overline{\\nu}_\\text{e}$.)"
    }
